==========================================
SYSADMIN DAY 01 NOTES — tmux
Date: 14-10-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- tmux keeps a session alive even if the terminal app closes or an SSH connection drops
- Sessions (tmux new -s / tmux attach -t) are the top level; name them so they're easy to find
- Windows (Ctrl+b c) are like tabs inside one session; panes (Ctrl+b % or ") split one window
- Detach with Ctrl+b d; everything keeps running in the background until you reattach
- tmux ls shows every session and whether it's currently attached
- This matters most on a remote server over SSH, where a dropped connection would normally kill anything running

COMMANDS / ACTIONS I PRACTICED:
[ ] tmux new -s <name> / tmux ls / tmux attach -t <name>
[ ] Ctrl+b d (detach) and reattaching
[ ] Ctrl+b c, rename with Ctrl+b , , switching windows with n/p
[ ] Ctrl+b % and " (splitting into panes), moving between them
[ ] Ctrl+b z (zoom)
[ ] closing the whole terminal app while something ran inside tmux, then reattaching
[ ] tmux kill-session -t <name>

